---
// Four ways to close a motor case, in half section: a bolted flange, a lock ring, radial pins and a thread. Each shows
// the thin case membrane, the thick joint ring, the closure, the part that carries the end load, the seal and the
// pressure. Schematic, not to scale.
const ink = 'var(--rd-ink)', muted = 'var(--rd-muted)', steel = 'var(--rd-steel)', load = 'var(--rd-warn)', seal = 'var(--rd-accent)', hot = 'var(--rd-hot)';
const AX = 190, BORE = 70, RING = 50, MEM = 62; // local y: axis, bore, outer surface of the joint ring and of the membrane
const panels = [
  { x: 0, y: 0, title: 'Bolted flange', cap: 'bolts carry the load in tension' },
  { x: 220, y: 0, title: 'Lock ring', cap: 'a ring in shear, in two grooves' },
  { x: 0, y: 210, title: 'Radial pins', cap: 'pins in shear through the wall' },
  { x: 220, y: 210, title: 'Threaded', cap: 'the thread carries it in shear' },
];
// case wall: membrane, taper, joint ring to the end of the case at x = end
const caseWall = (end: number) => `M8,${MEM} L52,${MEM} L64,${RING} L${end},${RING} L${end},${BORE} L8,${BORE} Z`;
const arrows = (x: number, ys: number[]) => ys.map((y) => `M${x - 26},${y} L${x - 3},${y} M${x - 9},${y - 4} L${x - 3},${y} L${x - 9},${y + 4}`).join(' ');
const thread = Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, k) => `${116 + k * 4},${BORE + (k % 2 ? -4 : 0)}`).join(' L');
---

<figure class="viz closure-types">
  <p class="viz-title">Four ways to close a motor case</p>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 440 420" role="img" aria-labelledby="ct-desc" style="max-width: 620px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <desc id="ct-desc">
      Four half sections of the end of a motor case. In each, the thin case wall thickens into a joint ring at the end,
      the pressure pushes the closure out of the case, and one part carries that end load into the case. A bolted flange
      carries it in bolts in tension, with a face seal inboard of the bolts. A lock ring sits half in a groove of the
      case and half in a groove of the closure and carries it in shear. Radial pins go through the joint ring and a
      skirt of the closure, in shear. A threaded closure carries it in the thread. In the last three, a radial seal on
      the closure sits on the pressure side of the joint.
    </desc>
    {panels.map((pn, k) => (
      <g transform={`translate(${pn.x},${pn.y})`}>
        <rect x="2" y="2" width="216" height="204" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="var(--rd-line)"></rect>
        <text x="110" y="18" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" fill={ink}>{pn.title}</text>
        <line x1="8" x2="212" y1={AX} y2={AX} stroke={muted} stroke-dasharray="10 3 2 3" stroke-width="0.8"></line>
        <text x="26" y="132" font-size="12" font-style="italic" fill={hot}>p</text>
        {k === 0 && (
          <g>
            <path d={`${caseWall(150)} M140,24 L150,24 L150,${BORE} L140,${BORE} Z`} fill={steel} fill-opacity="0.85"></path>
            <rect x="150" y="24" width="14" height={AX - 24} fill="var(--rd-blue)" fill-opacity="0.4" stroke="var(--rd-blue)"></rect>
            <line x1="132" x2="172" y1="36" y2="36" stroke={load} stroke-width="3"></line>
            <rect x="128" y="31" width="6" height="10" fill={load}></rect>
            <rect x="170" y="31" width="6" height="10" fill={load}></rect>
            <circle cx="150" cy="61" r="3" fill={seal}></circle>
            <path d={arrows(150, [104, 136, 168])} fill="none" stroke={hot} stroke-width="1.6"></path>
          </g>
        )}
        {k === 1 && (
          <g>
            <path d={caseWall(150)} fill={steel} fill-opacity="0.85"></path>
            <rect x="92" y={BORE} width="80" height={AX - BORE} fill="var(--rd-blue)" fill-opacity="0.4" stroke="var(--rd-blue)"></rect>
            <rect x="128" y={BORE - 10} width="8" height="20" fill={load}></rect>
            <circle cx="104" cy={BORE + 3} r="3" fill={seal}></circle>
            <path d={arrows(92, [104, 136, 168])} fill="none" stroke={hot} stroke-width="1.6"></path>
            <line x1="100" x2="100" y1="38" y2={RING - 2} stroke={muted}></line>
            <text x="100" y="34" font-size="10" fill={muted} text-anchor="middle">joint ring</text>
            <line x1="30" x2="30" y1="44" y2={MEM - 2} stroke={muted}></line>
            <text x="30" y="40" font-size="10" fill={muted} text-anchor="middle">membrane</text>
          </g>
        )}
        {k === 2 && (
          <g>
            <path d={caseWall(150)} fill={steel} fill-opacity="0.85"></path>
            <path d={`M62,${BORE} L172,${BORE} L172,${AX} L112,${AX} L112,${BORE + 12} L62,${BORE + 12} Z`} fill="var(--rd-blue)" fill-opacity="0.4" stroke="var(--rd-blue)"></path>
            <rect x="84" y={RING - 6} width="7" height={BORE + 12 - RING + 6} fill={load}></rect>
            <circle cx="70" cy={BORE + 3} r="3" fill={seal}></circle>
            <path d={arrows(112, [110, 140, 170])} fill="none" stroke={hot} stroke-width="1.6"></path>
          </g>
        )}
        {k === 3 && (
          <g>
            <path d={caseWall(150)} fill={steel} fill-opacity="0.85"></path>
            <rect x="96" y={BORE} width="76" height={AX - BORE} fill="var(--rd-blue)" fill-opacity="0.4" stroke="var(--rd-blue)"></rect>
            <path d={`M${thread}`} fill="none" stroke={load} stroke-width="2.4"></path>
            <circle cx="104" cy={BORE + 3} r="3" fill={seal}></circle>
            <path d={arrows(96, [104, 136, 168])} fill="none" stroke={hot} stroke-width="1.6"></path>
          </g>
        )}
        <text x="110" y="202" font-size="10" fill={muted} text-anchor="middle">{pn.cap}</text>
      </g>
    ))}
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The case in grey, the closure in blue, the part that carries the end load in amber, the seal in red and the chamber
    pressure p. In each, the case gets thick at the end: the joint ring carries the groove, the holes, the thread or
    the flange, and the seal. In the last three, the seal sits on the pressure side of the joint, so the holes and the
    grooves are not part of the pressure boundary.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
